# Shell scripts and anything a Linux box executes must keep LF endings.
# A CRLF shebang makes the kernel look for an interpreter called "bash\r",
# and the installer would fail on every machine with "bad interpreter" —
# invisibly, since the file looks fine in an editor.
*.sh            text eol=lf
Dockerfile      text eol=lf
Caddyfile       text eol=lf
*.yml           text eol=lf
*.yaml          text eol=lf
*.sql           text eol=lf
